<figure class="not-prose render-plan" aria-label="Pixel renderer pipeline schematic">
  <figcaption><span>Rendering decision</span><strong>Keep the style. Preserve depth.</strong></figcaption>
  <ol>
    <li><span class="rp-number">01 / COLOR</span><h4>Build the pixel image</h4><p>Pixelated scene → output conversion → color quantization</p><div class="rp-swatch rp-coarse" aria-hidden="true"></div></li>
    <li><span class="rp-number">02 / DEPTH</span><h4>Rebuild occlusion</h4><p>Clear depth. Render visible geometry with color writes disabled.</p><div class="rp-swatch rp-depth" aria-hidden="true"><span>Near</span><span>Far</span></div></li>
    <li><span class="rp-number">03 / ARTWORK</span><h4>Draw the sharp layer</h4><p>Selected artwork stays crisp and obeys the new depth buffer.</p><div class="rp-swatch rp-sharp" aria-hidden="true"><i>CHAI</i><b></b></div></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="rp-caption">Pipeline schematic, not render-target captures. Extra full-resolution passes add work; pixel styling alone establishes no speed gain.</p>
</figure>

